<title>JAPAN: Mitsubishi Corp awaiting U.N. okay on oil deal.</title>
<headline>Mitsubishi Corp awaiting U.N. okay on oil deal.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsubishi Corp said on Wednesday that it expects the United Nations to approve its 40,000 barrels-per-day (bpd) contract to buy Iraqi crude oil within the next few days.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect to receive approval from the United Nations within the next couple of days,&quot; a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>She said the contract, covering a period of 90 days, had been sent to the United Nations shortly after it was concluded last week.</p>
<p>Mitsubishi is acting as an agent for five Japanese oil companies, Japan Energy Corp (JOMO), Nippon Oil Co Ltd, Kashima Oil Co Ltd, Showa Shell Sekiyu KK and Mitsubishi Oil Co Ltd.</p>
<p>Industry sources said the companies had not yet fixed a tanker to lift the crude.</p>
<p>Earlier, industry sources said it was proving to be a major task to adjust the schedules of the various companies.</p>
</text>
